# Problem-2:
Name="Srikar"
# indexing=positon-1
print(Name[2]) #gives output as i.
print(Name[1:3]) # 1 is included and 3 is exculded.so ri.
print(Name[ :3]) # it starts from zero and ends at 3 (Sri).
print(Name[0:]) # it starts from zero and goes until last index so(Srikar).
print(Name[-1:-6]) # it starts from last as Python moves left → right by default, but here start is greater than end, so nothing is printed
print(Name[ : : 2]) # it starts from zero and continous till last by leaving 2 position so(0,2,4-S,i,a)
print(Name[-6:-1])
"""Start index = -6 → S
End index = -1 → r (excluded)
Step = +1 (default)
So Python prints characters from -6 up to -1 (not including -1)."""
print(Name[-1:-6:-1]) # output will be rakir



Concept that must be learnt.
Step	Meaning
1	move forward normally
2	skip one character
3	skip two characters
-1	reverse direction
-2	reverse and skip one
Example Program:
Name = "Srikar"

print(Name[::1])   # Srikar
print(Name[::2])   # Sia
print(Name[::-1])  # rakirS
print(Name[::-2])  # rkr


